        "original_id": "773c0896-23ae-5bca-bc6c-a04f9fff67e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Union Pacific Railroad, Clinchfield Railroad, Chesapeake and Ohio Railway, Yancey Railroad\n- Places: Dante, Virginia, Elkhorn City, Sandy Ridge Mountains, Kona, North Carolina, Micaville, Burnsville\n- Concepts: Challenger locomotives, railroad connections, freight service\n\nFacts:\n- In 1915, the Clinchfield Railroad completed a 35-mile segment from Dante, Virginia, to Elkhorn City.\n- The 1915 Clinchfield Railroad segment opened coal lands north of the Sandy Ridge Mountains and formed a connection with the Chesapeake and Ohio Railway at Elkhorn City.\n- Challenger locomotives were most common on the Union Pacific Railroad and the Clinchfield Railroad.\n- The Yancey Railroad was an American Class III shortline railroad with reporting mark YAN.\n- The Yancey Railroad operated freight service for 10.6 miles from a connection with the Clinchfield Railroad at Kona, North Carolina, through Micaville, to Burnsville.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
